Time Complexity:
O(log n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Count how many multiples of 5 are present from 1 to n.
2. Add n/5 to the answer since each multiple contributes at least one factor of 5.
3. Divide n by 5 repeatedly to count extra factors contributed by powers like 25, 125, etc.
4. Keep adding the quotient to the count until n becomes 0.
5. Return the total count of trailing zeroes.



class Solution {
    public int trailingZeroes(int n) {
        int count = 0;
        while(n!=0){
            count+=n/5;
            n/=5;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
